# OpsFlow request samples — VS Code (REST Client), Visual Studio and Rider run this file directly.
# Start the stack first (README "Run it locally"), then set the password from SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD in your .env.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@password = <your SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD>

### 1. Sign in as an employee
# @name employeeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "employee1@opsflow.local", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Create a draft request (Idempotency-Key makes retries safe)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-create-1

{ "title": "New laptop", "description": "Replacement for a 5-year-old machine", "category": "Purchase", "amount": 1450.00 }

### 3. Submit it: If-Match must carry the ETag from the previous response (412 if stale, 428 if missing)
# @name submitted
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests/{{created.response.body.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
If-Match: {{created.response.headers.ETag}}

### 4. Sign in as the employee's manager and open the approvals inbox
# @name managerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "manager1@opsflow.local", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approvals/inbox
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Read the request as the manager (fresh ETag) and approve the current step
# @name forManager
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests/{{created.response.body.id}}/steps/{{forManager.response.body.steps[0].id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
If-Match: {{forManager.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "Approve", "comment": "Approved: within the team budget." }

### 6. Audit history of the request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests/{{created.response.body.id}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Lists: filter, sort and page (sort fields: createdAt, updatedAt, amount, reference; '-' = descending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests?status=Approved&sort=-amount&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. An error, to see the problem-details shape (unknown sort field → 400 validation.failed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/requests?sort=title
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
